diff --git a/doc-build/md062.md b/doc-build/md062.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..5804e529
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc-build/md062.md
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+This rule is triggered when a code block has more lines than the `maximum`
+parameter allows (for example, with `maximum` set to `2`):
+
+````markdown
+```text
+One
+Two
+Three
+```
+````
+
+To fix this, shorten the code block or split it into smaller ones.
+
+A code block's length is its number of content lines: for a fenced code block,
+the lines between the opening and the closing fence (blank lines included);
+for an indented code block, all of its lines.
+
+Note: With the default value of `0` for `maximum`, there is no limit and this
+rule never reports a violation.
+
+Note: The `ignore_languages` parameter lists languages (the first word of the
+info string, compared without regard to case) whose fenced code blocks are not
+checked.
+
+Rationale: Long code blocks are hard to read; shorter examples are easier to
+follow.
